+# Phase 6.1: Embedding Fine-Tuning Pipeline - Research
+
+**Researched:** 2026-11-24
+**Domain:** domain adaptation of a multilingual (zh/en/it) dense retriever; synthetic query generation; hard-negative mining; contrastive training; safe model rollout on pgvector profiles; data governance in multi-tenant RAG
+**Confidence:** HIGH on the codebase findings and the sentence-transformers API (fetched 2026-11-24); MEDIUM on recipe hyper-parameters (literature defaults, need the live run); LOW on the size of the gain over a hosted Qwen3-8B production profile (unknown until the live run).
+
+## User Constraints (from CONTEXT.md)
+
+Locked decisions D-01..D-33 in `06.1-CONTEXT.md`. Open PO questions 1–8 have defaults adopted. Deferred: a per-tenant global profile pointer, LoRA on large models, non-1024 slots, cross-encoder filtering, consent UI, continual training.
+
+## Phase Requirements
+
+| ID | Description (short) | Research support |
+|----|----|----|
+| FT-01 | Per-tenant opt-in consent, deployment-only scope, revocation taints models | §Governance, F-6, F-7 |
+| FT-02 | Tenant-scoped corpus export with document-level split and golden decontamination | F-3, F-8, Pattern 2 |
+| FT-03 | Synthetic queries, ~3 per chunk, zh/en/it, structured, budgeted | F-4, Pattern 3 |
+| FT-04 | Filters: answerability, verbatim n-gram, near-duplicate, with report | Pattern 4 |
+| FT-05 | Real mined pairs from 5.1.1 (`TrainingPair`), decontaminated, up-weighted | F-16 |
+| FT-06 | Hard-negative mining with production model or ST model; margins; FN guards and audit | §sentence-transformers, Pattern 5 |
+| FT-07 | Reproducible GPU training kit; CachedMNRL default; CPU tests | Pattern 6 |
+| FT-08 | Offline eval vs base and production; EMB-05 gate unchanged | Pattern 7 |
+| FT-09 | Fine-tune slots, OpenAI-compatible provider, probe check, re-embed, flip/rollback, 3.1.1 bindings | F-1, F-2, F-5, F-15, Pattern 8 |
+| FT-10 | Model registry and versions; retention and prune | Pattern 9 |
+
+## Project Constraints (from CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md)
+
+- New `.env.local` names mirrored in `scripts/init-env.js`, `src/lib/env.ts`, `scripts/config-server.js`, `scripts/config-ui/index.html`, `scripts/rag/env-manifest.json` (`node scripts/check-config.mjs`); secrets classified in `scripts/config-server-security.js`.
+- Every component has a switch; off = today's behaviour (D-02).
+- Pydantic v2 is the source of truth, Zod generated (`npm run gen:schemas`, CI `git diff --exit-code` in `.github/workflows/pr-smoke.yml:136-139`).
+- All retrieval/embedding use goes through `@/lib/rag` (`scripts/ci/check-rag-boundary.mjs`).
+- SECURITY DEFINER rules (search_path `''`, revoke/grant, allow-list, two tests).
+- No secrets or real data in the repo; fixtures synthetic only.
+- Prove effect against the baseline; real items gate when they exist (EVAL-14).
+
+## Summary
+
+The repository already has everything a fine-tuned model needs to go live *safely*: side-by-side profiles in `chunk_embeddings` with a partial HNSW index per profile (`0308_chunk_embeddings.sql:22-35`), a resumable, tenant-scoped re-embed job (`0315`, `npm run rag:reembed`), and an activation gate that refuses incomplete, mixed-model, unproven or stale profiles (`0309_profile_activation.sql:11-113`) fed by `rag_record_eval_evidence` (`0318`). What is missing is (1) the training-data pipeline, (2) the trainer and its offline evaluation, (3) a provider that can serve a model nobody hosts publicly, and (4) governance (consent, registry, revocation, retention).
+
+The recommended design keeps the gate untouched and adds **two fixed fine-tune slots** (`ft-a-1024`, `ft-b-1024`) whose HNSW indexes are created once by migration. A model version is bound to a free slot, re-embedded, evaluated and activated exactly like any other profile; the next version uses the other slot (blue/green). This avoids dynamic DDL in a SECURITY DEFINER function, keeps "never mix vectors" structural (one model per slot, bind refused while the slot has rows), and makes rollback the existing pointer flip.
+
+The production model is hosted (OpenAI 3-small or Qwen3-8B on DeepInfra), so it is not a sentence-transformers model and cannot be passed to `mine_hard_negatives`. The default miner therefore reuses the production vectors already stored in the database plus query vectors computed through `@/lib/rag`, and reimplements `mine_hard_negatives`' filtering semantics in NumPy (parity-tested against the library on a tiny model). That also lets mining run on this CPU-only machine.
+
+**Primary recommendation:** sentence-transformers 6.2.0 (pinned; 6.3.0 was published 2026-11-11, inside the two-week freshness window), `CachedMultipleNegativesRankingLoss` with mined hard negatives and `NO_DUPLICATES` batching on `Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B` (zero-shot compared with bge-m3 and multilingual-e5-large-instruct first), relative margin 0.05, document-level 80/10/10 split with golden-test documents held out, offline gate then the EMB-05 gate on the real golden set.
+
+## Codebase Findings (file:line)
+
+- **F-1 Profiles are deployment-wide, one active.** `embedding_profiles` with a partial unique index on `status = 'active'` (`supabase/migrations/0307_embedding_profiles.sql:10-28`); RLS on, service role only (`:48-50`). Consequence: a globally active model serves every tenant; tenant-private models therefore go through 3.1.1 bindings (F-15, D-33), never the global pointer. REQUIREMENTS Out of Scope "Per-tenant provider choice" (`.planning/REQUIREMENTS.md:184`) confirms.
+- **F-2 HNSW indexes are static per profile.** `chunk_embeddings_<profile>_hnsw ... USING hnsw ((embedding::halfvec(N)) halfvec_cosine_ops) WITH (m = 64, ef_construction = 200) WHERE profile_id = '<id>'` (`0308_chunk_embeddings.sql:24-35`). No code creates indexes at run time (`grep -rn "hnsw" src/lib/rag scripts` finds none). → fixed slots (D-22).
+- **F-3 Activation gate** checks completeness, `embedding_model`/dims consistency, evidence target, baseline = current active, `gate_passed`, `pre_migration`, completed backfill run of the target, evidence newer than the data (`0309_profile_activation.sql:11-113`). Rollback restores `previous_active_id` if it still has a vector for every current ready chunk (`0309:116+`). Phase 7 plans `0705/0706_activation_gate_external` also extend it → this phase must not redefine it (D-25 uses triggers instead).
+- **F-4 Existing LLM drafting.** `eval/src/rag_eval/draft/claude_drafter.py:1-60` (Anthropic tool-use, Pydantic `DraftedItemBatch`, trilingual, persona styles), `eval/config/draft.json` (model id, languages), `eval/pyproject.toml` extra `draft` (`anthropic==2.12.0`). `SupabaseWorkspaceSource` (`eval/src/rag_eval/draft/sources.py:79-...`) already reads one tenant's chunks with the service key and refuses ambiguous single/multi-tenant scopes (`:112-131`). Reuse both.
+- **F-5 Providers are keyed by provider id with one static model.** `getEmbeddingProvider(id)` (`src/lib/rag/embeddings/registry.ts:37-41`), `validateProfileShape` with `MAX_HALFVEC_DIMS = 4000`, `MAX_VECTOR_DIMS = 2000` (`registry.ts:15-16, 56-66`), `EmbeddingProviderId = 'openai' | 'voyage' | 'qwen3'` (`types.ts:1`), startup check compares `provider.model` with `profile.model` (`active-profile.ts:291-299`) and key presence (`active-profile.ts:277-286`). → one provider id per slot whose `model` is the env-configured version id (D-23); the existing EMB-03 checks then work unchanged.
+- **F-6 Qwen provider shape to copy** (OpenAI SDK against a custom base URL, retries, abort, exact-dims check, `EmbeddingProviderError` without vendor body): `src/lib/rag/embeddings/qwen.ts:86-180`.
+- **F-7 Old-style search_path on 0318/0309** (`SET search_path = pg_catalog, public`); 0411 fixed listed functions. New functions use `SET search_path = ''` (brief).
+- **F-8 Split helper** `eval/src/rag_eval/split.py:11-14` is item-level (golden items); the fine-tune split is a new document-level rule with its own rule string (D-10).
+- **F-9 Bounds and paired stats** exist: `eval/src/rag_eval/bounds.py` (Clopper-Pearson), `paired.py`, `profile_compare.py` (builds `EmbeddingProfileComparison` and `ActivationEvidence`, `rag-sidecar/src/rag_sidecar/contracts/profiles.py:41-70`).
+- **F-10 Re-embed CLI** `npm run rag:reembed -- --profile <id> [--dry-run] [--tenant] [--derive-from]`, `--resume`, `--rollback` (`src/lib/rag/ingest/reembed/cli.ts:21-25`); `--derive-from` is same-model MRL only, not applicable to a new model.
+- **F-11 Latency budget**: `embed` stage 200 ms for chat/embed/voice (`eval/config/latency-budgets.json:4-40`).
